# The published site is only what lives under version control here. Source
# material can sit in this folder for convenience without being deployed.
# Anything meant to go live belongs in /assets/ (documents) or /images/
# (photography), committed under a clean lowercase name.

# Local tooling state
.netlify/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# OS and shell cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
nul

# Source archives and working folders. These hold the originals the site is
# built from, including multi-hundred-megabyte photo sets that GitHub rejects.
/5 Spheres of Empathy/
/5 Spheres of Empathy Books/
/Global Sustainability Tours/

# Working documents, wherever they end up
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.pptx
*.key
*.zip

# Loose originals dropped at the repo root. The published copies of these
# already exist under /assets/ and /images/ with clean names.
/*.pdf
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.png
!/og.png
!/Mr_G_headshots_ZuzannaGerulewiczPhotography_06.jpg

# Source PDFs parked in page directories rather than /assets/
/field-notes/*.pdf

# Extracted course content. This repo is PUBLIC and Netlify serves the repo
# root, so anything committed here is world-readable. The lesson pages under
# /bsfp-accelerator/ are deliberately public and indexed; what stays out is the
# raw extraction the pages were built from, which is not fit to publish.
/course-export/

# Carousel and social artwork. Source art for LinkedIn, sized and cropped for
# that feed rather than for the site, and heavy. The published copies of any
# image used in a field note live in /images/field-notes/ under a clean
# lowercase name; this folder is where they were cut from.
/field-notes/*carousel*/

# Client-facing pitch pages. These are written for one organisation and shared
# by direct link, not published. Committing one puts it on the live site and
# into the public git history for good.
/pah-pitch/

# Blank certificate templates. These are fillable and must never be published at
# usable resolution; only the small previews in /bsfp-accelerator/ go live.
/bsfp-accelerator/Certificates/

# The site gained a functions directory, so it gained a dependency tree.
# Netlify installs it at build time from package-lock.json.
node_modules/

# Dropped by the Netlify CLI when it inspects functions. Not ours.
deno.lock

# Working notes, strategy documents and session records. Everything committed to
# this repository is deployed to a public web host, so internal material stays
# out of it. These rules also exist on the drill-schema branch; duplicated here
# deliberately so the protection does not depend on which branch merges first.
ops-log/
Course Core Competencies/

# Skill Drill decks. Facilitator material — timings, chat prompts, the run of
# the room — and this repository deploys to a public web host, so they stay
# local. See skilldrills/decks/README.md.
skilldrills/decks/

# Google Drive leaves this behind while syncing.
.tmp.driveupload/

# Sales and marketing source material. Mural exports, decks and working PDFs.
# This repository is public, so the originals stay local.
/5 Spheres Sales and Marketing/

# Social film build artefacts. Frame sequences run to roughly 1.4GB per cut and
# this directory syncs to Google Drive, so they are deleted after encoding and
# rebuilt on demand: see video/sick-day/README.md. Frames are a pure function of
# time, so a rebuild is byte-identical and render.py --resume picks up where an
# interrupted run stopped. The finished MP4s stay out of the repository too,
# because everything committed here is deployed to a public web host.
video/*/frames/
video/*/assets/
video/*/stills/
video/*/_verify/
video/*/_chrome_profile/
video/*/out/
video/*/contact_*.png
video/*/verify_*.png

# Vendored agent skills installed by `npx skills add`. Third-party material, and
# not something to publish with the site.
.agents/

# Self-contained local previews. Built by scratchpad/_selfcontained.py so a page can be
# looked at from disk without a server running. Megabytes of inlined fonts, never deployed.
/PREVIEW-*.html

# Local environment files. Nothing with a token in it goes near this repository:
# the publish directory is the repository root, so a committed .env is not just
# in the history, it is downloadable at /.env on the live site. Local values for
# netlify dev belong here or on the command line, never in a tracked file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
